  faqs: [
    { question: "Where do I even start looking for an IB tutor in Mandsaur?", answer: "Start by writing to us with the programme, subject, level and exam session, since that brief is what actually drives the shortlist, not a location search. Mandsaur district runs no IB Diploma, MYP or PYP classroom of its own, so a specialist is found nationally and then fitted to your evening routine, never the reverse. Every match opens with a free trial lesson, and a different tutor gets offered if the first one is not right." },
    { question: "Are there tutors for Cambridge or Edexcel IGCSE serving Mandsaur students?", answer: "Yes, both boards are covered. Whichever specification a child's boarding school has set, Cambridge or Edexcel, the tutor gets matched to that exact code and tier, teaching entirely online since no in-person option is offered in Mandsaur. Mathematics 0580 Extended and Chemistry 0620 come up often, and preparation runs against each board's actual past papers rather than generic revision material." },
    { question: "Will someone actually come to our house in Mandsaur for lessons?", answer: "No, nobody visits a Mandsaur home for this. House calls exist only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR, and everywhere else, Mandsaur very much included, the lesson happens live online with a shared screen standing in for a shared table. It is a private one-to-one class delivered at home through a laptop, not a claim that a tutor walks through your door." },
    { question: "What kind of fee should we expect for tutoring in Mandsaur?", answer: "It comes down mostly to scarcity: IB Diploma Higher Level subjects cost more nationally than Cambridge IGCSE Core work, purely because fewer tutors teach the former well. Session length, the subject and how recently a tutor has taught that specific syllabus all factor in too, and the number gets confirmed in writing before your trial starts, with no travel charge added and no contract binding you afterward." },
    { question: "Is there genuinely no IB or IGCSE school in Mandsaur?", answer: "Correct, none is confirmed. CBSE schools such as Shree Dalauda Public School and St Thomas Senior Secondary School, and State Board schools such as Dashpur Vidyalaya, cover most of the city, and even Mandsaur International School runs the State Board despite its name. Indore and Udaipur, both around 150 kilometres away, hold the nearest confirmed IB and Cambridge schools." },
    { question: "My son boards at an international school outside Mandsaur. Does tutoring during holidays make sense?", answer: "It is one of the more frequent requests we get from this city, precisely because no local school runs the IB or Cambridge curriculum. A tutor works against whichever exact subject, level and syllabus the boarding school teaches, fitting sessions into school breaks or, if the school permits it, agreed slots during term itself." },
    { question: "Do you genuinely not charge for the first class?", answer: "That is correct, the opening lesson costs nothing and asks for no commitment. A child works through a real topic with the tutor over video, and only afterward does a short plan for the coming month arrive, which a family can accept, question or use as a reason to try a different tutor altogether." },
    { question: "Can an IB Internal Assessment get help from a Mandsaur-matched tutor?", answer: "Yes, within a firm limit: a tutor guides, they do not write. That covers shaping a workable research question, unpacking what each criterion is actually looking for, planning how evidence gets gathered, and reacting honestly to a draft. Producing or rewriting the assessed text itself would break IB integrity rules, so it is refused outright." },
    { question: "Which Diploma subjects does IB Gram actually cover for families here?", answer: "The major DP subject groups are all covered: both Maths routes, Analysis and Approaches and Applications and Interpretation, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, together with Theory of Knowledge and the Extended Essay, matched at whatever HL or SL level a Mandsaur-linked boarding student actually needs." },
    { question: "Is tutoring available for MYP and PYP students too, not just the Diploma?", answer: "Yes, the full continuum is covered for Mandsaur households whose child studies abroad or at a boarding school on any IB stage. MYP work leans on criterion-based analysis across sciences and languages, plus the Personal Project journal, while PYP sessions build reading fluency, number sense and the research habits an Exhibition later needs." },
    { question: "Can an online tutor really substitute for someone in the room in a city like Mandsaur?", answer: "In practice, yes, and arguably more so here than in a city with its own IB school, since the alternative locally is close to nothing and no in-person tutor for these subjects exists in Mandsaur anyway. A shared screen, live-marked past papers and recorded worked examples cover most of what sitting beside a tutor would otherwise offer, while opening the search to specialists across India rather than a handful of local names." },
    { question: "How does IB Gram check who it puts in front of a Mandsaur student?", answer: "Each tutor is checked on qualifications, on how recently they have actually taught the exact subject and level in question, and on how they handle assessment criteria, before ever meeting a family. Given the total absence of a local IB or IGCSE school, preference goes to someone who has taught that specific syllabus recently, and the trial lesson lets you confirm the fit yourself." },
    { question: "Is there a right time to begin IB or IGCSE tutoring from Mandsaur?", answer: "The cleanest start is at the beginning of the course itself, Grade 9 for IGCSE or Class 11 for the Diploma, which leaves room to fix gaps before internal exams and predicted grades start piling up. A later start, even in the final year, can still move the needle, just with the plan narrowed to the highest-value topics and timed practice." },
    { question: "We are considering a move from CBSE or the MP Board to IGCSE. Would a tutor help with that switch?", answer: "It is a common enough request among Mandsaur families weighing a boarding move around Grade 9. Content is rarely the real obstacle; the shift is mostly about question style, since command words like 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' expect a different kind of answer, and that is best taught a term ahead of the actual switch." },
    { question: "Does session timing work around Mandsaur's own calendar, mandi season included?", answer: "It does. Weekday evenings and weekend mornings are the usual slots, shifted earlier in the peak Malwa heat when families prefer it, and kept deliberately flexible during the November-to-January mandi rush for households whose evenings get unpredictable then. A second weekly slot before mocks or an exam series is easy to add." },
    { question: "What if the tutor we get is not the right match for our Mandsaur student?", answer: "Tell us and a replacement gets found, no argument needed. Check-ins every few weeks exist specifically to catch a mismatch early rather than let it drag on for a term, and since there is no long contract in the first place, pausing or ending sessions never carries a penalty." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram tied to any Mandsaur school, or to the IB and Cambridge organisations themselves?", answer: "No, IB Gram operates independently and holds no affiliation with, endorsement from or representation of any school mentioned on this page, nor with the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel. Schools appear here only to describe where Mandsaur families actually board, and tutors follow each school's own calendar and syllabus." },
  ],

